{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cfdvk4QWofWmA52Ce9Dn6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe audit logging is bolted into the responder step, which breaks the one-step-one-responsibility idiom this codebase is built on.\n\n- `RespondWithOwnerCreated` is, per the naming conventions in AGENTS.md, a `RespondWith<E>Created` step whose job is to map the entity to a DTO and send the 201. It now does two unrelated things: respond *and* emit an audit record. The audit emission is a distinct side effect, not part of responding.\n- The idiomatic structure here is a separate step in the pipeline — e.g. an `AuditOwnerCreated` function class wired with `next:` ahead of the responder (reading the owner via `@Val Owner`). That keeps each class single-purpose, makes the audit step independently testable/reorderable, and matches how the rest of the endpoints compose small steps rather than accreting behavior into one class.\n- As written, the responder is on its way to becoming a catch-all: the next cross-cutting concern (metrics, events) would likely get dropped in here too, since there's now precedent. Pulling audit into its own step avoids that drift.\n\nThe logger definition itself (dedicated `AUDIT` channel, static final, documented) is fine — it's the *placement* of the emission that should move to its own pipeline step."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9193,"cache_read_input_tokens":11894,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9193},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"556f00a9-8490-4a92-9328-7018af56dcaf","uuid":"0c535515-560b-49b4-b474-8b66fce67db3","timestamp":"2026-10-02T19:01:49.50